hich from the user's perspective looks like nothing happened since the window was already invisible on their screen. They expect Fn to show the window, but it goes hidden instead, matching their complaint that the toggle \"serves no purpose.\" The real issue is that the toggle should check if the window is key (frontmost and focused) rather than just visibility—if it's key, hide it; otherwise show and activate it. This handles all cases: a hidden window appears, a window behind others comes to front, and a focused window disappears. The user also wants a Dock icon option since the menu bar is getting crowded and the ChatGPT menu item is hidden behind an overflow menu, so I need to switch the activation policy to show it in the Dock instead of keeping it menu-bar-only.\n\nThe implementation plan is to change the activation policy to .regular for the Dock icon, implement the Dock reopen handler to show the window when clicked with no visible windows, fix the toggle logic to use isKeyWindow, and potentially keep both the Dock icon and menu bar item for redundancy.…","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1515,"cache_read_input_tokens":285125,"output_tokens":2473,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1515,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2473,"cache_read_input_tokens":285125,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1515},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdveAeDZpKGbUJNrqh1yk","type":"assistant","uuid":"e38ecf86-0b4d-456b-a2df-2045a3a77597","timestamp":"2026-08-11T08:25:49.769Z","effort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Me