roach is to disable the window shadow entirely and rely on the CSS box-shadow already present in the page's own styling for the visual effect.\n\nNow I'm moving on to implementing Cmd+D for dictation control.\n\nI'll expose a function that searches the DOM for either a start or stop dictation button by matching aria-labels, then clicks whichever one exists — this keeps it stateless and always reflects what's actually on the page. The Swift side will call this from the AppDelegate's Cmd+D handler through the webView.\n\nFor the interaction design, I'm thinking Cmd+D should handle dictation control only: show the window if it's hidden, then toggle between starting and stopping dictation. The Fn key already handles showing and hiding the window independently, so keeping these concerns separate makes the most sense — Cmd+D drives the dictation state while Fn manages window visibility.\n\nNow I'm implementing this: I'll add regex-based matching in bridge.js to reliably identify the start and stop buttons (avoiding hardcoded labels), create a `__zrToggleDictation` method, and add a corresponding `toggleDictation()` method in ChatWindow.swift that manages the dictation state…","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1597,"cache_read_input_tokens":323871,"output_tokens":6183,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1597,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6183,"cache_read_input_tokens":323871,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1597},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdvfM2as5HsXKBq1j23PD","type":"assistant","uuid":"64d22e07-444c-4e1b-9298-085e30cfdc47","timestamp":"2026-08-11T08:41:58.336